<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Shiga Pref. on Misa's Odekake Blog</title><link>https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/tags/shiga-pref./</link><description>Recent content in Shiga Pref. on Misa's Odekake Blog</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 30 Aug 2017 00:00:00 +0900</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/tags/shiga-pref./index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Azuchi Castle Ruins</title><link>https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/azuchi-castle/</link><pubDate>Mon, 14 Aug 2017 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/azuchi-castle/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Azuchi Castle Ruins.
This was the castle of famous feudal warlord Nobunaga Oda.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are only stone walls and stairs were left, but I guess it is what is called decadentism, the place has a nice atmosphere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From the tower ruin, you can overlook the townscape and the lakescape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/images/azuchi-castle2.jpg" alt="" width="780" height="520"&gt;
 
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;figure&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/images/azuchi-castle3.jpg" alt="" width="780" height="520"&gt;
 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!--
安土城跡観光に行きました。
あの有名な織田信長のお城です。
石垣と階段しか残っていなかったけど、いわゆる廃墟の美というやつでしょうか、雰囲気があって良かったです。
天守台近くからの長めは、町と湖が一望できて良かったです。

I went sightseeing to the Azuchi Castle Ruins. This is famous Nobunaga Oda's Castle.
Only stone walls and stairs were left there, I guess it is what is called decadentism, the place had a nice atmosphere.
The view near by the tower ruin was good to overlook the townscape and the lakescape.
--&gt;</description></item><item><title>Kawachi Wind Cave</title><link>https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/kawachi-wind-cave/</link><pubDate>Mon, 14 Aug 2017 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/kawachi-wind-cave/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I entered Kawachi Wind Cave.
The inside of the cave is very cool regardless of summer!
I thought there is likely Blue Grotto, Italy, but underground lake was keep out area.
Well, it was nice to feel the power of nature even just in the public open area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/images/kawachi-wind-cave2.jpg" alt="" width="520" height="780"&gt;
 
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;figure&gt;
 &lt;img src="https://odekake.zzzmisa.com/images/kawachi-wind-cave1.jpg" alt="" width="780" height="520"&gt;
 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!--
河内風穴に行きました。
夏にもかかわらず中は涼しい！
青の洞窟見たいなのが見られるかと思ったら、地底湖は立ち入り禁止でした。
でもまあ一般公開されている部分だけでも、自然の力を感じられてよかったです。

I entered Kawachi Wind Cave.
Inside of cave is very cool regardless of summer!
I thought I can see a sight likely Blue Grotto Capri, but underground lake was keep out area.
Well, it was nice to feel the power of nature even just in the public opened area.
--&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>